  "notes": "{激怒|げきど} describes the most extreme level of anger — violent, explosive fury beyond ordinary {怒|いか}り.\n\nINTENSITY SCALE:\n- {怒|おこ}る / {怒|いか}る: to be angry (general)\n- {立腹|りっぷく}する: to get upset (formal, moderate)\n- {激怒|げきど}する: to be furious (intense, explosive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{激怒|げきど}している means 'is furious' — describes the ongoing state of being enraged.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {激怒|げきど}を{買|か}う: to incur someone's fury\n- {激怒|げきど}させる: to enrage someone\n- {激怒|げきど}して{席|せき}を{立|た}つ: to leave one's seat in a rage\n\nREGISTER:\nMore commonly used in written language, news reports, and formal contexts than in casual conversation. In everyday speech, めちゃくちゃ{怒|おこ}る or ブチ{切|ぎ}れる are more natural.",
